-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material


This software contains material derived from five projects by Evan Czaplicki,
all licensed under the same BSD 3-Clause License reproduced above. Their
copyright notices are retained here, as clause 1 requires, and apply to the
files listed under each. Everything not listed -- the compiler, the JavaScript
runtime and virtual DOM engine, and the remaining prelude modules -- is
dartea's own work.


elm/core -- https://github.com/elm/core
Copyright 2014-present Evan Czaplicki

    lib/prelude/packages/core/Basics.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/Char.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/Dict.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/List.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/Maybe.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/Result.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/core/Tuple.elm

A program that imports these modules is compiled alongside Basics.mjs,
Char.mjs, Dict.mjs, List.mjs, Maybe.mjs, Result.mjs and Tuple.mjs, and
redistributing that output redistributes material derived from elm/core.


elm/html -- https://github.com/elm/html
Copyright (c) 2014-present, Evan Czaplicki

    lib/prelude/packages/html/Html.Attributes.elm

A program that imports Html.Attributes is compiled alongside
Html.Attributes.mjs, and redistributing that output redistributes material
derived from elm/html.


elm/browser -- https://github.com/elm/browser
Copyright 2017-present Evan Czaplicki

    lib/prelude/packages/browser/Browser.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/browser/Browser.Events.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/browser/Browser.Navigation.elm

The module names, types and signatures are reproduced; the update loop,
navigation and event machinery are dartea's own. A program that imports these
modules is compiled alongside Browser.mjs, Browser.Events.mjs and
Browser.Navigation.mjs, and redistributing that output redistributes material
derived from elm/browser.


elm/url -- https://github.com/elm/url
Copyright 2017-present Evan Czaplicki

    lib/prelude/packages/url/Url.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/url/Url.Builder.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/url/Url.Parser.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/url/Url.Parser.Internal.elm
    lib/prelude/packages/url/Url.Parser.Query.elm

These modules are reproduced nearly verbatim. A program that imports them is
compiled alongside the matching .mjs files, and redistributing that output
redistributes material derived from elm/url.


elm/http -- https://github.com/elm/http
Copyright 2014-present Evan Czaplicki

    lib/prelude/packages/http/Http.elm

The types, the request builders and the response resolution are reproduced;
the transport is dartea's own. A program that imports Http is compiled
alongside Http.mjs, and redistributing that output redistributes material
derived from elm/http.


evancz/elm-todomvc -- https://github.com/evancz/elm-todomvc
Copyright (c) 2014-2016, Evan Czaplicki

    playgrounds/todomvc/Main.elm

The file is the upstream TodoMVC application, kept as a test that dartea
compiles a real Elm program. Only `infoFooter` and its call are removed;
nothing else is changed. It is a test fixture, not part of the compiler, and is
not redistributed in compiled output.
